consider the meta_preproc* files.

they frequently use the following pattern:

sb_printf(&op_buffer,
          "{%s, 0, 0, 0, {%u, %u, %u, %u, ",
          type_str, mask[0], mask[1], mask[2], mask[3]);
sb_printf(&op_buffer,
          "%u, %u, %u, %u}},\n",
          mask[4], mask[5], mask[6], mask[7]);

which makes it kind of hard to see where a generated { has its matching }.
Please try to make use of the following pattern (only where there are more than
1 sb_printf() calls in a row):

SB_APPEND(&out, "{");
sb_printf("%s, .field = %d,", var);
sb_printf(".other_field = %d,", other_var);
SB_APPEND(&out, "}");

so that at least some of the brackets are separated from the values.
Dont apply the pattern everywhere, only in some places, so I can see that you
got the idea right).
